page=f'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>061 · Variable-depth fracture valleys</title><style>{css}</style><header><h1>061 · Variable-depth fracture valleys</h1><p>The same proof camera, now shown both untextured and fully shaded in the alley. The crack bottoms vary with the opening width: opposing slopes converge into a valley instead of stopping at one flat depth plane.</p><p><a href="#comparison">Same-camera comparison</a> · <a href="#before">Depth change</a> · <a href="{a}scene.blend">Editable scene</a></p></header><section id="comparison"><h2>Identical camera · two views</h2><p>Camera position, rotation, projection, framing and resolution are identical. The left view isolates the gray mesh under a proof light; the right restores the surrounding scene, materials and scene lighting.</p><div class="grid">'+fig(a+'panel-clay.png','061 · untextured, lit geometry')+fig(a+'panel.png','061 · fully shaded in scene')+'</div></section><section id="before"><h2>From a flat floor to converging walls</h2><div class="grid">'+fig('/art/reviews/xenon-060/panel-clay.png','060 · fixed-depth recessed floor')+fig(a+'panel-clay.png','061 · varying valley depth')+'</div><p>At each surface point, the depth limit is set by its distance from the nearest opening edge and a 55° inward wall envelope. Smooth local variation stays within that limit. This is a sampled geometric approximation of converging walls, including at junctions; there is no uniform bottom plane or separate floor overlay.</p></section><section><h2>Support</h2>'+fig(a+'support.png','061 · same depth rule on the concrete support')+'</section><section><h2>Game camera</h2>'+fig(a+'render.png','061 · unchanged alley camera and two-component scope')+'<p>Both evaluated cut components pass the closed-mesh check. Reference direction: UP-01, UP-03, DP-08 and the supplied concrete closeup. User review pending.</p></section></html>'
(P/'review-061.html').write_text(page);(P/'index.html').write_text(page)
